 ## Overview
-Shading models for volume rendering enhance the perception of 3D structure and surface orientation in scalar field data by applying local illumination heuristics [S1, unofficial]. Unlike physically based light transport methods that solve the radiative transfer equation, this method modulates the existing volume samples or pixel colors using diffuse and specular terms derived from the data gradient [S2, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from siblings like [Gradient-based Shading with Phase Functions](1020-gradient-based-shading-with-phase-functions.md) by using a simplified Phong-like heuristic rather than phase functions, and from [Frequency Domain Directional Shading](852-frequency-domain-directional-shading.md) by operating in the spatial domain [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
+Shading models for volume rendering enhance the perception of 3D structure and surface orientation in scalar field data by applying local illumination heuristics [S1, unofficial]. Unlike physically based light transport methods that solve the radiative transfer equation, this method modulates the existing volume samples or pixel colors using diffuse and specular terms derived from the data gradient [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from frequency domain methods by operating directly in the spatial domain using explicit vector math [S1, unofficial].
 
